Below are the tables and the logical relationships.

─────────────────────────────  
1. Goals Table

| Name               | Text                                                                                                           | Runtime                                        | Goal Type | Target Condition / Enquired Information | Relation |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|-----------|------------------------------------------|----------|
| G1: Complete Mission | Complete the mission of collecting required resources from storage and delivering them to the requesting agent. | OR(G2;G3, G4)                                  | Achieve   | All required resources are delivered.   | OR       |
| G2: Collection Phase | Collect the required resources from storage.                                                                  | FALLBACK(AT1;AT2;AT3, AT4;AT5)                   | Achieve   | Resource is retrieved from storage.     | Fallback |
| G3: Delivery Phase   | Deliver the collected resources to the specified location.                                                    | FALLBACK(AT6;AT7, FALLBACK(AT8;AT9, AT10))        | Achieve   | All resources are delivered to location. | Fallback |
| G4: Parallel Execution | Execute multiple collection‐delivery tasks in parallel using multiple robots.                                | AT11;AT12                                      | Perform   | N/A                                      | AND      |

─────────────────────────────  
2. Tasks Table

| Name                | Text                                                                                               | Relation | Location           | Number of Robots |
|---------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|--------------------|------------------|
| AT1: Navigate Storage | Navigate to the storage location where the resource is located.                                 | AND      | Storage            | [1]              |
| AT2: Request Resource | Send a message to the storage with the precise specification of the requested resource.           | AND      | Storage            | [1]              |
| AT3: Wait for Retrieval | Wait until the resource is retrieved from storage.                                             | AND      | Storage            | [1]              |
| AT4: Navigate Recharge | Navigate to the recharging station due to low battery during collection.                         | AND      | Recharging Station | [1]              |
| AT5: Reassign Mission  | Reassign the collection mission to another robot.                                              | AND      | Recharging Station | [1]              |
| AT6: Navigate Delivery | Navigate to the specified delivery location.                                                   | AND      | Delivery Location  | [1]              |
| AT7: Deliver Resource  | Deliver the collected resource to the requesting agent.                                         | AND      | Delivery Location  | [1]              |
| AT8: Return to Checkpoint | Return the resource to a designated checkpoint due to low battery during delivery.              | AND      | Checkpoint         | [1]              |
| AT9: Reassign Delivery  | Reassign the remaining delivery task to another robot.                                         | AND      | Checkpoint         | [1]              |
| AT10: Trigger Alert     | Trigger an alert and send a report to the sector manager if checkpoint delivery fails.           | AND      | Checkpoint         | [1]              |
| AT11: Assign Robots     | Assign multiple robots for parallel collection‐delivery tasks.                                 | AND      | Control Center     | [1]              |
| AT12: Execute Parallel  | Execute the assigned collection‐delivery tasks in parallel.                                    | AND      | Various            | [2,5]            |

─────────────────────────────  
3. Logical Relationships

- **G1 → G2, G3, G4**  
  • G1 (Complete Mission) is decomposed into two alternative branches:  
  – The single‐robot branch (G2 and G3 executed sequentially)  
  – The parallel multi‐robot branch (G4)  
  • Runtime: OR(G2;G3, G4)  
  • Relation: OR (fulfilling one branch is sufficient)

- **G2 → AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4, AT5**  
  • G2 (Collection Phase) has a primary branch (AT1;AT2;AT3) and a fallback branch (AT4;AT5) activated when the battery is low.  
  • Runtime: FALLBACK(AT1;AT2;AT3, AT4;AT5)  
  • Relation: Fallback (binary fallback between normal and low‐battery handling)

- **G3 → AT6, AT7, AT8, AT9, AT10**  
  • G3 (Delivery Phase) has a primary branch (AT6;AT7) and a fallback branch (AT8;AT9) for low battery during delivery.  
  • If the fallback branch fails, AT10 is executed.  
  • Runtime: FALLBACK(AT6;AT7, FALLBACK(AT8;AT9, AT10))  
  • Relation: Fallback (nested fallback for handling checkpoint failure)

- **G4 → AT11, AT12**  
  • G4 (Parallel Execution) is decomposed into two sequential tasks: first assign robots (AT11) then execute the tasks in parallel (AT12).  
  • Runtime: AT11;AT12  
  • Relation: AND (both tasks must be executed)

